`maps=true` on a target compiles cleanly. No source-map sidecar is emitted
yet -- no platform reads Request.Maps until Plan B -- but the option must not
cause a compile error, which is what the golden being the ordinary page says.

-- main.sngl --
import . "sngl:ui"

output {
    none {
        html(maps=true)
    }
}

component main {
    text(value="hello")
}
-- out/none/html/index.html --
